{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785087920,"nonce":"r77bGosD9/h14MA17oGjUzDBk3k=","title":"`ui/scarab-docs-ui/src/content/docs/usage/pipeline-syntax.mdx` documents","message":"`artifacts:` but says **nothing** about how a step publishes a **result**. There is\nno mention of `/scarab/results/` anywhere in the docs site.\n\nThis is not a cosmetic gap — it let a silent data-loss bug live in our own sample\npipeline (fixed in PR #91).\n\n\n- Results are written as **`/scarab/results/\u003cname\u003e.json`**, and the result NAME is\n  the filename minus `.json`.\n- The file must hold **valid JSON**: `\"abc123\"` for a string, `42` for a number —\n  not bare text.\n- The trusted egress sidecar drains **`*.json` only** (`for f in *.json` in\n  `docker/sidecar/scarab-results-egress.sh`).\n- They are then read downstream as `${{ outputs.\u003cstep\u003e.\u003cname\u003e }}`.\n- A `build:` step emits an `image` result natively via BuildKit\n  `--metadata-file /scarab/results/image.json` — the author writes nothing.\n\n\nWriting a bare `/scarab/results/tag` — the obvious guess, and what\n`.scarab/dogfood.yaml` did from the day it was written — publishes **nothing**.\nThe glob matches no file, the sidecar logs only `no results to drain`, and **the\nstep still exits 0**. The run goes green while `${{ outputs.version.tag }}`\nsilently resolves to empty downstream. Nothing anywhere tells the author they\nproduced no result.\n\n\nA `results:` section in pipeline-syntax.mdx alongside the existing `artifacts:`\none, drawing the contrast explicitly: **results are small typed values the DAG\ninterpolates; artifacts are files you download afterwards.** Include a worked\nexample of writing a string and a number, and state the exits-0-on-typo trap\noutright — plus the advice that a consumer should assert its interpolation\nresolved (`test -n \"$VAR\"`), which is what turns the silent no-op into a failure.","files":null}]}